# This is committed test data, not somebody's workspace.
#
# `workspace.ensure()` writes a .gitignore here the first time any command runs
# against this directory, and the one it writes excludes `cache/` -- correct for
# a real installation, where the cache is derived and refetchable. Here the raw
# files ARE the fixture: they are the frozen input the goldens are computed
# from, and they have to be committed.
#
# `ensure()` only writes the file when it is missing, so this one existing is
# what stops it. Deleting it would not fail anything loudly -- the next fixture
# added would simply never be committed, and the suite would pass locally and
# fail on a clean checkout.
#
# What genuinely is derived here is listed in tests/fixtures/.gitignore.
